# Keep the build context — and therefore the image — free of secrets and junk.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY backend/ ./backend/`, which takes *everything* in
# that directory. On a developer machine that includes backend/.env (now
# carrying TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY and GROQ_API_KEY) and the IND Money OAuth token
# cache. Both are gitignored, so a CI build from a clean checkout never saw
# them — but a local `docker build` would bake them straight into a layer.
# This file is what stops that.

# --- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.env
!**/*.env.example
**/.ind_money_token.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*

# --- vcs / tooling state --------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.agents
.temp
.superpowers

# --- python ---------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
.venv
venv
env
ENV
build
dist
**/*.egg-info

# --- frontend (never enters the backend image) ----------------------------
frontend
**/node_modules
**/.next

# --- RAG corpus + vector store (dormant since C1; not copied anyway) -------
data

# --- docs / plans ---------------------------------------------------------
docs
*.md
!README.md

# --- os junk --------------------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
